; specs/turbobaby/legacy_retirement.t27 -- what "retired" means in this repository
; This contract owns one distinction and nothing else: DATA that was hidden is not the same
; thing as a SURFACE that is still reachable. It is the contract for DECISIONS.md D5 and D19
; and for the open issue #2 under epic #26. It states the three partial retirement states this
; tree actually exhibits, the one completed state that makes them legible, the rule that a
; hidden row never retires a live surface, and the allowlist mechanism D19 and epic #26 both
; require -- heritage is hidden rather than deleted, and anything kept is named with a reason.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-21). The two retirement migrations disagree about what retirement is,
; and no contract said so. That absence was RE-MEASURED on 2026-09-21 against the finished
; 43-file corpus and it still holds, but only in its narrow form, so the narrow form is what is
; written: 16 of the other 42 files now contain the word "retire", and NONE of them declares the
; distinction this file owns. The grep that decides it is not the word but the state machine --
; retirement_state, STATE_DATA_HIDDEN and STATE_SURFACE_LIVE appear in no other file. The 16 are
; something else: the edge REUSES_LEGACY_RETIREMENT_ID pointing here, the bike-unit STATUS
; "retired" that turbobaby/availability owns, and the retired "skate" spelling that
; turbobaby/ride-game and turbobaby/star-award own. A reader who greps the WORD gets 16 and must
; not read that as sixteen contracts ruling on retirement; the word is shared, the subject is not.
; (Re-measured 2026-09-22 over the 45 files the corpus now holds: the word reaches 19 of the other
; 44, and the distinction is still declared in none of them. "Appear in no other file" was already
; too strong on 2026-09-21: the note above CORPUS_FILE_COUNT has both readings and the one file
; that names retirement_state without declaring it.)
; migrations/083_drop_cannabis_catalog.sql drops six tables outright
; (:82-84 and :88-90). migrations/085_unpublish_woody_catalog.sql deletes no row and drops no
; table: it issues six visibility UPDATEs (:25-30) and one in-place rename (:36-38), and says
; at :12 and :19-21 that the rows are kept and the flags are reversible. Underneath both, the
; surface never moved. src/api/mod.rs:89 still merges the legacy catalog router, whose routes()
; at src/api/catalog.rs:13-59 declares 27 HTTP routes over accessories, accessory sets, tea
; products, tea sets and strain sets -- routes whose tables now answer with rows that were
; flipped invisible, not removed. src/ui/routes.rs still declares eight legacy paths that
; resolve to legacy screens. So the live count that forces this file is a ZERO: of the eight
; legacy screen routes and the 44 legacy HTTP routes measured below, migrations 083 and 085
; retired NONE. They were data decisions, and a data decision cannot retire a surface.
; (Re-measured 2026-09-22: the HTTP figure is 43, not 44. 2c21df1 removed the quest router's
; /api/test registration on 2026-09-21, after this paragraph was written -- a code change, not a
; data decision, so the paragraph's point stands: 083 and 085 moved none of the 43. Whether an
; unreachable test endpoint counts as a completed retirement is not re-decided here, and
; COMPLETED_RETIREMENT_COUNT is unchanged. The correction is recorded above the HTTP counts.)
; --
; The sharpest single measurement is the allowlist. tests/retired_table_wiring.rs:49-83 (:49-82 until 2026-09-26) holds
; four entries excusing shipped code that still reads a table 083 dropped. All four name the
; SAME table, strains -- so one of the six dropped tables carries every surviving reader and
; the other five carry none. That is the third state: the table is gone, the reader is not,
; and what keeps the tree honest is not the drop but the named excuse.
; --
; WHERE THE BRIEF IS REFUTED (four survey citations opened and checked on 2026-09-21).
;   1. "about 23 routes" in src/api/catalog.rs:16-58 is 27. A count of route declarations in
;      that file returns 27, and every one of them is inside routes(); the declarations span
;      :16-58 and the function spans :13-59. The count is pinned below as 27.
;   2. "/game renders a cannabis-era shop title to any customer who opens it (src/ui/game/
;      shop_game.rs:1)" does not survive its own citation. Line 1 of that file is a SOURCE
;      COMMENT, which no customer can see. The component's rsx root at src/ui/game/
;      shop_game.rs:679 (:596 since the farm zone left that file on 2026-09-26) opens with a coin HUD and declares no title node at all, and the one
;      title key the repository defines for this screen family, T_GAME_TITLE at
;      src/trios/i18n.rs:345, resolves to a TurboBaby string in both locales (:1010 and :1610,
;      re-pinned 2026-09-25 after a key declared above them moved both rows) and is
;      referenced by no screen -- a search for T_GAME_TITLE under src/ returns only i18n.rs
;      itself. A search of src/ui/game/shop_game.rs for a quoted string carrying the old shop's
;      name returns zero. What IS true, and is what this contract counts, is coarser and worse:
;      the ROUTE is live. src/ui/routes.rs:64 declares /game, :285 mounts GameScreen, src/ui/
;      screens/game_screen.rs:15 mounts the legacy component, and 1957 lines of a shop-and-
;      planters game render to any customer who opens the path. The surface is the defect; the
;      title was not.
;   3. "tests/retired_table_wiring.rs, survey :49-81" is :49-82 -- the const opens at 49 and
;      closes at 82 (at 83 since 2026-09-26, when a survivor's reason grew a line). The size, 4, is what this file pins, not the span.
;   4. "about 9523 LOC across 26 of the 181 src/*.rs files". 181 was right: every .rs file under
;      src/ counted to 181 on 2026-09-21 (corrected 2026-09-22: 182 since src/trios/order_status_view.rs was added that day; 187 since five files arrived on 2026-09-26, re-measured 2026-09-29 at 55a6664). 9523 across 26 does not reproduce -- no TRACKED file in the tree
;      carries the number 9523, and no nameable file list sums to it. This file therefore pins
;      its OWN reproducible measurement instead: 25 named legacy-domain source files totalling
;      9193 lines, the set being the eight screens behind the live legacy routes, the four UI
;      game modules and the set card, the three API modules that serve them, five entities, and
;      the four trios and db modules of the strain, quest, tea and pack domains. A number whose
;      file list cannot be named is not evidence, so 9523 is reported unconfirmed, not copied.
;      (2026-09-29: the 25 were described here and never printed until that day. They are printed
;      as LEGACY_SOURCE_FILES near the end of this file; the 9193 reproduces exactly at d1877db,
;      the commit that wrote this paragraph, and the same 25 paths sum to 8840 at 55a6664.)
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It implements no route, describes no screen, carries no Cyrillic
; copy and names no deletion date -- issue #2 is open and the order of retirement is the
; owner's call, refused explicitly below. It restates nothing a sibling owns: the delivery-zone
; rename that rides along in the same migration 085 belongs to turbobaby/delivery-terms, which
; owns ZONE_RENAME_MIGRATION and ZONE_ROWS_KEPT_REASON, and is neither re-decided nor counted
; here; the mount status of the orphaned catch asset belongs to turbobaby/game-score, which owns
; CATCH_ERA_ASSET_IS_MOUNTED; the retirement of the skate spelling belongs to turbobaby/ride-game
; and turbobaby/star-award, the latter owning RETAINED_LEGACY_SOURCE, so no /skate path enters
; any count below; and the word "retired"
; as a BIKE UNIT STATUS is turbobaby/availability's, which owns STATUS_RETIRED and STATUS_NAMES, a
; different subject that this file never touches. Each sibling is named by ID and declaration
; rather than by line: all three of these were line citations, all three still pointed at the
; right subject on 2026-09-21, and all three would have rotted on the next edit next door. It carries no renter, handle, phone, key
; code, plate, debt, purchase price or personal note (D14): every constant here is a table
; name, a path, a route pattern or a count.
; (2026-09-29: "describes no screen" is kept as the rule and narrowed by one thing. From that day
; this file NAMES every legacy file no contract named -- 21 of them -- and records for each how it
; is built, whether a customer reaches it in this file's own states, and the counts, routes, keys
; and literals a gate can check. That is evidence for a classification, not a description of what
; a screen should do: no surface is re-decided, no copy is proposed, and every defect the naming
; found is recorded as a measured, dated fact and left unfixed -- this round changed no code.)
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-legacy-retirement;

