pub fn next_surface_is_decided_here(owner_has_ranked: bool) bool {
    return false;
}

; --- The owner's ruling of 2026-09-24: rental only, Phuket only ----------------------------------
; The owner ruled on 2026-09-24 that a customer may only RENT a bike, and only in Phuket. Events and
; bike sales leave every customer surface; the referral programme, loyalty and the ride game stay.
; Rows are kept -- a placed order may carry a sale line and a booking may name an event, and both
; must keep reading -- so the target is a surface no customer reaches, and never a dropped table.
; The two surfaces the ruling was briefed as naming, events and bike sales, are not among the eight
; above. Whether "rental only" also reaches any of the eight is NOT settled here: two of them,
; /accessories and /tea, take orders for goods, which is not a rental, and the question is put to
; the owner rather than answered by this file. So NEXT_SURFACE_NOTE stays true of the eight -- no
; ranking of them exists yet -- and this file still picks nothing.
; Each ruled surface is run through this file's own machine on its OWN inputs, because they are not
; the same. The events rows are hidden: 085 and migrations/088_unpublish_events.sql flip
; events.is_public, and the admin API can publish none (turbobaby/events-booking), so events are
; retirement_state(false, false, false, true), STATE_DATA_HIDDEN. No bike-sale row is hidden: the
; stored sale flag and asking price are untouched and the admin list still serves them; what
; changed is that the public catalog reads mask them (turbobaby/catalog-api) and the order path
; refuses a new sale line (turbobaby/commerce). Fed that true input, the machine answers
; retirement_state(false, false, false, false), STATE_LIVE, and the input is not bent to reach
; another state: none of the five states names a mask on read, and STATE_LIVE here says only that
; no data was hidden and no table dropped, not that a customer reaches the offer. Whether a mask on
; read deserves a state of its own is this file's open question, recorded, not decided. Either
; way surface_is_retired answers false for both, and that is not smoothed over:
; here "retired" means STATE_FULLY_RETIRED, which needs a dropped table, and the owner forbade the
; drop. So nothing in the corpus may claim either surface is GONE -- may_claim_surface_is_gone needs
; zero route, handler and screen declarations, and the event paths in REPOINTED_ROUTE_COUNT stay
; declared on purpose -- and COMPLETED_RETIREMENT_COUNT stays 1. What each surface answers today is owned
; elsewhere and named by ID: the events surface by turbobaby/events-booking, the public catalog wire
; by turbobaby/catalog-api, the order path by turbobaby/commerce.
pub const OWNER_RULING_AT : str = "2026-09-24";
pub const OWNER_RULING_NOTE : str = "Rental only, Phuket only: events and bike sales leave every customer surface; the referral programme, loyalty and the ride game stay; no row is deleted and no table is dropped.";
