; --- The owner's answer of 2026-09-25: the eight legacy paths -------------------------------------
; The owner answered a numbered list of questions in chat on 2026-09-25. Answer 7 was a yes to this
; proposal: the old non-rental client addresses -- the previous shop's goods, its game and its hunts
; -- open the catalog; the ride game, referrals and loyalty stay; and the quest a customer opens from
; the profile loses its minimum-purchase line. Seven of the eight LEGACY_PATHS_DECLARED fall under
; it: /accessories and /tea (goods), /game (the previous shop's game; the kept ride is /ride, which
; is none of the eight), /treasure-hunt, /ar-hunt and /location-quest (the hunts), and /tech-tree.
; The answer's words name the goods, the game and the hunts, not the tech tree: /tech-tree -- a
; development tech tree, no rental and none of the three things the answer kept -- is counted among
; the old non-rental addresses on THIS FILE'S READING of the answer, and OWNER_ANSWER_NAMES_THE_TECH_TREE
; says so, so that the owner can overrule it. Each stays declared and its handler in
; src/ui/routes.rs -- fn Accessories, fn Tea, fn Game, fn TreasureHunt, fn ArHunt, fn LocationQuest,
; fn TechTree -- renders the live catalog; the seven screens stay compiled and exported and no
; handler mounts them (tests/rental_only_wiring.rs pins both ends, the unmount and the export).
; --
; The eighth is kept. /quest/:id is where the profile's quests row goes (the Link to Route::Quest
; with the id "daily" in src/ui/screens/profile_screen.rs), and the answer kept that row and removed
; one line from the screen behind it: T_PURCHASE_MIN, the previous shop's minimum purchase. The
; screen is kept as the answer asked and is not re-decided or described here. The key stays
; translated, as the retired buy-out keys do; no screen renders it, nor T_PURCHASE_REQUIRED and
; T_ERROR_PURCHASE beside it, which no screen rendered before either. No sentence was written new:
; a line was removed, which is the whole of the copy change, and this paragraph is its record.
; --
; Each path is run through this file's machine on its OWN inputs, as the ruling of 2026-09-24 was.
; No customer reaches any of the seven screens now. /accessories and /tea read tables 085 hid
; (HIDDEN_TABLES), so they are ruled_surface_state(false, true), STATE_DATA_HIDDEN; the other five
; read no table 085 hid, so they are ruled_surface_state(false, false), STATE_LIVE, which here says
; only that no data was hidden and no table dropped, as it did of bike sales. The kept quest is
; reachable, so it is STATE_SURFACE_LIVE by this file's precedence, kept on purpose and named with
; its reason, which is what D19 asks of anything kept. None is a completed retirement: no table was
; dropped and COMPLETED_RETIREMENT_COUNT stays 1.
; --
; WHAT THE ANSWER DID NOT MOVE. The HTTP routes behind the seven paths stay merged: the legacy
; catalog, quest and tech-tree routers still answer LEGACY_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT routes, and the quest
; router is also what the kept quest scans through. Whether any of them should stop answering is not
; in the answer and is not decided here. The deep-link compatibility set grew by the seven paths;
; that set is turbobaby/deeplink's (LEGACY_ROUTE_ALIASES) and is not restated here. The previous
; shop's game credited Stars under a source of its own (src/ui/game/shop_game.rs, the credit_stars
; closure); with its screen unmounted the ride is the one mounted screen that posts a Star credit,
; and whether that source stays capped is turbobaby/star-award's CAPPED_SOURCES, untouched here.
