; --- The owner's answers of 2026-09-26 on what answer 3 left in sight -------------------------------
; Questions about what answer 3 above still left in customers' sight were put to the owner on
; 2026-09-26. Each answer is quoted verbatim, in Russian, beside the code it moved, and this file
; stays ASCII.
;   * THE ORDERS (question 1). Read 1 above served a line of a retired kind under the neutral name.
;     Asked about those lines, the owner asked why they are there at all. The operator read it as:
;     a customer must not see the previous shop's orders at all. turbobaby/order-presentation
;     records the rule (PREVIOUS_SHOP_ORDER_*): an order naming the previous shop, or holding no
;     bike line, is neither listed, nor answered by id, nor counted on the profile. So reads 1 and
;     2 above now reach only an order holding a rental line beside a line of a retired kind, which
;     is this shop's and stays shown with that line masked. No row is written; the admin reads are
;     unchanged.
;   * THE MEDIA (question 3). The previous shop's media were still reachable by a direct link: files
;     under /uploads on the server's volume, and objects in the bucket. The owner asked what he
;     needs them for at all. The operator read it as: stop serving them; deleting the files is the
;     owner's own irreversible act and is not done here. turbobaby/upload-media records it
;     (OWNER_MEDIA_ANSWER_*, LOCAL_READ_*): the local read serves only a name a bike's picture
;     references, and the bucket, which this server does not serve and whose previous-shop keys no
;     code can tell apart, needs a production listing. Nothing is deleted.
;   * THE EVENT REMINDER (operator, the same day, under this answer 3). turbobaby/events-booking
;     had kept the 24-hour reminder for seats already held; every event is hidden since 088, so the
;     reminder mailed the previous shop's stored titles and venues. It now reminds public events
;     only (REMINDER_REVERSED_AT there); cancellation and refund of a held seat are unchanged.
;   * THE WELCOME CREDIT'S SENTENCE (critic note 5 under the rulings of 2026-09-25; its words are
;     the lane's interim choice and a question for the owner). Read 4 above withheld the welcome
;     credit's description because its sentence named the garden, and confirm_referral went on
;     writing that sentence into every new welcome row. Since 2026-09-26 it STORES the same sentence
;     with the garden's words dropped and nothing else changed (WELCOME_CREDIT_SENTENCE in the rules'
;     module); none of the four sentences already written fits the invitee's row
;     (WELCOME_SENTENCE_REUSES_ONE_OF_THE_FOUR). Neither the owner nor the operator worded it, and
;     this repository writes no customer copy of its own, so the sentence is a stored record and is
;     NOT served: read 4 withholds every welcome row's description, old or new, the described types
;     stay four (OWNER_ANSWER_3_DESCRIBED_TX_TYPE_COUNT), and a customer sees the generic label and
;     the amount until the owner supplies the wording (WELCOME_SENTENCE_AWAITS_THE_OWNER). A first
;     version served it and credited the words to the operator; the review of the round reversed
;     that the same day. No row is rewritten. LATER THE SAME DAY (R3) the owner retired the welcome
;     credit itself (turbobaby/referral-credit: the friend gets nothing), so no new welcome row is
;     written at all since (WELCOME_CREDIT_WRITERS, bound by gate 3); the sentence stays in the
;     rules for the rows already stored, and the question to the owner stands for those rows only.
;   * R1 AND R2, the owner's answers of 2026-09-26 to two reads the critic's pass left open
;     (verbatim in DECISIONS.md, "R1-R3, the owner's answers of 2026-09-26"). R1, of the loyalty
;     leaderboard (first names, total spend, tier, served to anyone): "only for the admin",
;     enforced in turbobaby/loyalty-ledger. R2, of three reads no mounted screen uses: "close it to
;     customers". The operator's reading: a caller without admin proof is answered EXACTLY as an
;     unmatched /api path is -- the same 404, JSON body and content type, the detail naming its own
;     path -- through one builder, crate::api::missing_route, which the fallback and
;     crate::api::admin_or_missing_route both call. An admin is served as before, the routes stay
;     registered (the config GET shares its path with the admin POST, and an unregistered GET would
;     answer 405), a failed attempt still counts toward the admin limiter, and no row is read or
