; --- The legacy footprint, printed and re-added (2026-09-29) --------------------------------------
; WHY (measured 2026-09-29 at 55a6664). A sweep that calls a file under src/ NAMED when its
; repo-relative path occurs anywhere in a .t27 found 187 .rs files under src/, 69 of them (6279
; lines) named by no contract. Twenty-one of the 69 are this file's subject. Eighteen are files of
; the 25 behind LEGACY_SOURCE_FILE_COUNT -- a list this header described on 2026-09-21 as one that
; "can be printed and re-added" and never printed, which is the defect SURVEY_LOC_CLAIM_NOTE
; refuses in someone else's figure. So it is printed here, in the header's own order: the eight
; screens behind LEGACY_PATHS_DECLARED, in that array's order; the four UI game modules and the set
; card; the three API modules whose routes make LEGACY_HTTP_ROUTE_COUNT; five entities; and the
; four trios and db modules of the strain, quest, tea and pack domains. The other seven of the 25
; were already named by a contract. Lines are counted as gate 3's line_count counts them (Python
; splitlines), at 55a6664 and, for the reading this file first took, at d1877db.
; --
; FIVE OF THE 25 MOVED, and none by a retirement: src/ui/screens/accessories_screen.rs 412 -> 396
; (52e08e5 on 2026-09-25, ruling #12's client half, and fb5913b on 2026-09-26, the leftovers),
; src/ui/game/quest.rs 295 -> 296 (8c25988, answer 7's purchase line became a comment),
; src/api/tech_tree.rs 283 -> 214 (2429012, the empty roadmap of ruling #12's server half),
; src/ui/game/shop_game.rs 1957 -> 1662 (fb5913b, the farm) and src/api/quest.rs 1097 -> 1123
; (5279b37, R2). No file of the 25 was deleted: COMPLETED_RETIREMENT_COUNT, seen from the source.
; --
; NOT THE WHOLE LEGACY SOURCE. Three files no customer reaches belong to this subject and are not
; among the 25: two components of the previous shop's goods -- the detail modal the goods screens
; and the set card open, and the admin set picker -- which the header's set left out while counting
; the set card beside them, and the module glue that still exports the seven repointed screens.
