; caller, and every row it could list sits in sets, accessory_sets or tea_sets, which 085 hid, so
; it answers an empty list. The machine does not read content, and fed that true input --
; reachable, rows hidden -- it answers STATE_SURFACE_LIVE: a hidden row never retires a reachable
; surface, this file's first rule, in one file. Its client callers are
; src/ui/components/set_card.rs:87 and :96, which nothing calls. PackBadge has four variants
; (:18-23) and four accepted stored values (:56-61), an unknown or empty value parses to none
; (:29-35), and six unit tests sit at :134-186. Its doc (:3) calls a pack a row of the sets table.
