; THE FIVE ENTITIES, each a SeaORM mirror of one legacy table, compiled with the server. Each runs
; through the machine as a reader and never as a surface: no customer reaches an entity except
; through a route that reads it.
;   * src/db/entities/strain.rs mirrors strains (DROPPED_TABLES[2]), 30 fields (:13-56). Three files
;     read it: src/api/cart.rs (:166 and :170, the cart line of kind strain), src/db/mod.rs
;     (:1043-1046) and src/db/strains.rs (:127 and :169). It is itself one of the four allowlist
;     paths (tests/retired_table_wiring.rs:51-52), so it is the STATE_READER_ALLOWLISTED case this
;     file already classified (RETIRED_READER_STATE_AFTER_THE_2026_09_25_RULING), not re-decided.
;   * src/db/entities/accessory.rs and src/db/entities/tea_product.rs mirror accessories and
;     tea_products (HIDDEN_TABLES[1] and [3]), 10 fields each; their one reader is the cart-line
;     lookup in src/api/cart.rs (:200 and :215), which keeps is_available rows only.
;   * src/db/entities/quest_place.rs mirrors quest_places, 9 fields, and has no reader. Whether the
;     entity guard excuses it is turbobaby/schema-provenance's ENTITY_GUARD_ALLOWLIST, which names it
;     today; the reason the guard's list gives is that src/api/quest.rs reads that table in raw SQL.
;     src/db/entities/treasure_hunt.rs mirrors treasure_hunts, 14 fields, has no reader either, and
;     is on no allowlist: it passes the guard on spelling alone, which is the same owner's
;     ENTITY_MODULES_PASSING_ON_SPELLING_ALONE_NAMES, through the word match its
;     ENTITY_GUARD_MATCHES_A_WORD_NOT_A_PATH records, at the one site its TREASURE_HUNT_ONLY_MATCH
;     names. MEASURED 2026-09-29 in both lanes: a false green in that guard -- an unwired entity
;     reads as wired -- recorded, not fixed. Neither table was hidden or dropped, and both public
;     reads over them answer customers the missing-route 404 since R2 (OWNER_R2_CLOSED_READS[0] and
;     [1]). CORRECTED 2026-09-30 (review of round 7): until then this bullet re-described the guard's
;     allowlist and word match in its own words, with their lines in src/db/mod.rs and
;     src/trios/i18n.rs; those facts are the guard owner's and are read here by the names above.
pub const LEGACY_ENTITY_FILES : [5]str = [
    "src/db/entities/strain.rs", "src/db/entities/accessory.rs", "src/db/entities/tea_product.rs",
    "src/db/entities/quest_place.rs", "src/db/entities/treasure_hunt.rs",
];
